  "title": "Bemelmans Bar",
  "indexDescription": "The Bemelmans Bar is a favorite place for us to visit in New York City.",
  "description": "The Bemelmans Bar is in the Carlyle Hotel on Manhattan's Upper East Side. It has old-world charm.  The walls were painted in 1947 by Ludwig Bemelmans in exchange for an 18-month stay in the hotel for his family. He is famous for writing and illustrating the children's book Madeline.\n\nWe have read Madeline many times to our kids.  The bar is a favorite and we try to visit every time we're in New York.",
